[31m-[m
[31m-## Phase A — Trainability (gate: must pass)[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Question:** Can JEPA train stably on LPS src→tgt pairs?[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Build**[m
[31m-- `CellTrajectoryJEPA` module: context encoder, EMA target encoder, time-conditioned predictor[m
[31m-- `JEPATrainer` Lightning module: latent MSE/smooth-L1 only[m
[31m-- CLI: `--train_mode jepa`, same LPS paths / GPUs `5,6,7`, sod2 outputs[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Train recipe**[m
[31m-- Init context encoder from masking ckpt; predictor random; EMA τ ≈ 0.996–0.999[m
[31m-- Predict one target time per step (or average over `pred_tps`)[m
[31m-- No token CE, no generation loop[m
[31m-[m
[31m-**Pass criteria**[m
[31m-- Train loss decreases; val loss tracks without NaNs[m
[31m-- Embedding variance stays non-collapsed (monitor `std(z)`, mean cosine sim)[m
[31m-- Sanity plot: UMAP of `z` separates time and/or cell type at least weakly[m
[31m-[m
